+---
+id: dl-002-inject-task-timestamp-source-at-the-public-boundary
+type: decision-log
+title: "Inject task timestamp source at the public boundary"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Context
+
+Tasks must expose ISO-8601 timestamps at creation and after every mutation. The domain rules forbid
+reading the wall clock, while tests must not depend on elapsed real time.
+
+## Decision
+
+`createTodoList` will obtain the current ISO-8601 timestamp through an optional, injected function
+that defaults at the public boundary to the system clock. It will pass that source to the domain task
+list. Creation reads the source once for both timestamp fields; each task mutation reads it once to
+set `updatedAt`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The domain remains deterministic when supplied a controlled timestamp source, and application callers
+can use the no-argument API. The public list factory gains an optional dependency for tests and other
+callers that need deterministic timestamps.
